   "cause": "A race, not a timeout. An exiting node process passes through /proc states the test helpers classify inconsistently: once its cwd link is released readProcessIdentity returns undefined (absent), and while its command line is empty but its state is not yet Z it throws private-process-identity-unreadable. The drain returned on its first empty scan, which could fall in the first window; afterEach's observation scan, which does not retry, could then fall in the second and throw. The afterEach failure leaves its observation unpushed, so afterAll's denominator is one short.",
